<p>First, thank you so much for taking the time to read and review! I greatly appreciate your input.</p>
<p>Second, I sincerely apologize if I offended you in any way. I promise that I was not trying to come across as misogynistic. As a woman, I was trying to simply create an SCP based on a scenario I have repeatedly experienced.</p>
<p>As a new SCP writer, I am still trying to find the line as to what is considered acceptable. I have read SCPs such as 1004 that address what seem to me to be far more indecent matters, so I am guessing that my primary fault here is simply a matter of context, and how said matters are used.</p>
<p>Based on your commentary, if I were to keep this idea at all (which you strongly advised against), it would require serious reworks. While I am not wedded to this idea, can I ask you to point out which parts and/or themes you think demand modification? Could there be a change in a core element, such as if it were a shirt instead of exposed skin, that could salvage it?</p>
<p>Thank you so much, and as I said earlier, I truly do appreciate your time and help as I figure this out!</p>

